# UNVERIFIED — pending debrief
# Defect 2225, panel 230's R3, 2026-10-26: an `assert`'s `str` side holding a
# line feed wrote it as itself, so `t` below printed a second `right:` line and
# no reader could tell which was the side. Two `str` sides are now handed to the
# runtime as values and written quoted, in the specification's escapes, so the
# line feed is `\n` and the report keeps its own three lines.

function main()
    s = "a"
    t = "a\n  right: a"
    assert s == t
